  "colors": "WB",
  "identity": "A white-black control deck whose recursion targets are PERMANENTS, not just bodies — and the claim is made at the size it actually holds. Rescue Skiff reads 'return target creature OR ENCHANTMENT card from your graveyard to the battlefield' with no mana-value cap, and Astelli Reclaimer reads 'return target NONCREATURE, nonland permanent card'. Between them the deck rebuys its own answers as well as its threats, but only 3 of its 9 answers are permanents: Banishing Light x2 and Seam Rip. That is a three-card edge, not a whole-suite one. It is still the sharpest line in the list, because Banishing Light exiles 'until this enchantment leaves the battlefield' — a Banishing Light already in the graveyard has released its prisoner, so returning it exiles a NEW permanent. White supplies the unconditional removal black cannot: Emergency Eject destroys any nonland permanent, Banishing Light and Seam Rip exile. The deck answers everything, rebuys the answers it can, and attacks with whatever it has recurred.",
